AgroPQ

An AI-Powered Crop Disease Detection and Agrochemical Recommendation Framework with Post-Quantum Secure Cloud Communication

Problem Statement

Modern agriculture faces significant crop losses due to plant diseases
and insect infestations. Manual disease identification is often
time-consuming, costly, and inaccurate, leading to delayed
treatment, reduced yield, and excessive agrochemical usage.

There is a need for an intelligent system that can detect crop
diseases from leaf images and recommend suitable pesticides,
insecticides, or fungicides based on the detected disease.

As smart farming increasingly uses cloud-based services, secure
agricultural data transmission is also important. Therefore, AgroPQ
aims to integrate AI-based disease detection, smart agrochemical
recommendation, and Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC)-based secure cloud
communication into a unified agricultural system.

I. Project Overview

1.1 Problem Context

Agricultural productivity is significantly affected by crop diseases and
pest infestations. Diseases caused by fungi, bacteria, viruses, and
insects can damage crops and reduce both yield and quality.

Traditional disease identification generally depends on:

Manual visual inspection

Farmer experience

Agricultural experts

Laboratory diagnosis

These approaches may not always be immediately available, particularly
for farmers who require quick decisions.

The proposed system uses machine learning and deep learning techniques
to analyze crop leaf images and identify diseases automatically.

After disease identification, the system provides suitable
treatment/agrochemical recommendations, including pesticides,
insecticides, or fungicides.

Since the system is intended to use cloud-based services, secure
communication is also considered. The proposed security layer
incorporates Post-Quantum Cryptography to address future quantum-related
security threats.

1.2 Motivation

1. Early Disease Detection

Early identification of crop diseases can help farmers take timely
corrective action and reduce crop losses.

2. Reduction of Manual Diagnosis

AI-based image analysis can reduce dependence on manual visual
inspection.

3. Smart Treatment Recommendation

Disease identification alone does not tell the farmer what action to
take. The system therefore aims to connect disease detection with
treatment/agrochemical recommendations.

4. Reduction of Unnecessary Agrochemical Usage

Appropriate recommendations can help avoid indiscriminate or unnecessary
pesticide usage.

5. Cloud-Based Agriculture

Modern agricultural applications can use cloud infrastructure for AI
processing, data management, and application services.

6. Future-Oriented Security

The increasing importance of quantum-resistant cryptography motivates
the inclusion of a Post-Quantum Security Layer.

1.3 Significance

The proposed system is significant because it attempts to connect three
important areas:

 Artificial Intelligence --- for automatic crop disease
detection.

 Smart Agrochemical Recommendation --- for providing treatment
recommendations based on detected disease.

 Post-Quantum Security --- for protecting agricultural data
transmission and cloud communication.

The overall objective is therefore not simply to create another
disease-classification model, but to develop an integrated smart
agriculture framework.

