II. Literature Review

2.1 Review of Relevant Research

The literature review for AgroPQ is divided into three major research
areas.

A. Crop Disease Detection

Research in agricultural AI has increasingly used machine learning and
deep learning to automatically identify crop diseases from plant images.

Common approaches

Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs)

Transfer learning

YOLO-based object detection

EfficientNet

Vision Transformers

Ensemble learning

Explainable AI

Existing research demonstrates that

Deep-learning models can learn disease-related visual patterns.

Image-based disease classification can automate diagnosis.

YOLO-based models can support detection-oriented applications.

Transformer-based approaches provide an alternative to traditional
CNN architectures.

Ensemble models can combine multiple models.

Explainable AI can help interpret model predictions.

Relevance to AgroPQ

AgroPQ will use this research as the foundation for its crop disease
detection module.

B. Agrochemical Recommendation

A second research area focuses on using machine learning for
agricultural decision support.

Existing research investigates

Crop recommendation

Fertilizer recommendation

Pesticide recommendation

Insecticide recommendation

Fungicide recommendation

Crop management

Agricultural input optimization

Possible inputs

Crop type

Disease

Soil parameters

Environmental conditions

Agricultural knowledge

Historical data

Limitation in Existing Approaches

Many recommendation systems are developed separately from image-based
disease diagnosis.

Relevance to AgroPQ

AgroPQ aims to connect:

Detected Crop Disease → Treatment/Agrochemical Recommendation

The system is intended to provide pesticide, insecticide, or fungicide
recommendations based on the detected disease.

C. Post-Quantum Cryptography and Cloud Security

The third research area concerns secure communication and post-quantum
cryptography.

Existing PQC research investigates quantum-resistant security for:

Cloud systems

IoT systems

Secure communication

Key establishment

Digital signatures

Data transmission

Proposed security technologies

ML-KEM

ML-DSA

PQTLS

Relevance to AgroPQ

The security layer is intended to protect communication involving:

User/application

Cloud platform

Agricultural database

Disease-analysis results

Recommendation results

2.2 Literature Synthesis

The collected literature indicates that substantial research already
exists in each individual area.

Crop Disease Detection

Deep learning has demonstrated strong potential for automatically
identifying crop diseases from images.

Agrochemical Recommendation

Machine learning can support agricultural decisions involving
fertilizers, pesticides, and crop management.

Post-Quantum Security

PQC provides a potential approach for protecting communication against
future quantum-enabled threats.

Overall Synthesis

However, these areas are generally investigated as separate technical
problems.

The literature therefore suggests an opportunity to integrate:

AI Disease Detection
        +
Agrochemical Recommendation
        +
Post-Quantum Security
        ↓
Unified Smart Agriculture Framework

